    {
      "id": "k1XllHUN2isrfzQHg6Z0m",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1328.808354367863,
      "y": 3181.955697396575,
      "width": 961.059326171875,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1072111574,
      "version": 671,
      "versionNonce": 1792317892,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786554006347,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "**** Rate limit strategy (Request and request)\n\n1. Simple large request ==> low request count ==> massive token use --> budget burned in one shot\n2. Tiny message ==> high request volume ==> Low token count --> system spam\n==> Use Redis for storage/token manage\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "**** Rate limit strategy (Request and request)\n\n1. Simple large request ==> low request count ==> massive token use --> budget burned in one shot\n2. Tiny message ==> high request volume ==> Low token count --> system spam\n==> Use Redis for storage/token manage\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "UUcdO99iqHTz3Nw2zw8zr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 275.52565035111934,
      "y": 5299.675406802716,
      "width": 1823.8585205078125,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1991261014,
      "version": 143,
      "versionNonce": 1324378564,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786554047024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** ChatGPT Model\n-- A Transformer model is used, where the system predicts natural sequences of words. \n-- The model is trained on internet data such as websites, books, and Wikipedia links to provide semantically meaningful and grammatically correct replies.\n\nThe model can use multiple approaches such as top K, greedy, or nucleus temperature to select the most accurate prediction.\n\n** Chatbot Design\n-- A dataset of question-and-answer pairs is initially used to train the model.\n\n-- However, since training the model on every possible question-and-answer combination is impossible, a reward model is designed to select the best responses.\n\n-- The reward model is also trained using reinforcement learning, where the chatbot is rewarded for giving appropriate responses and penalized for inappropriate ones.\n\n-- The chatbot design is expected to support different input and output formats, including images, audio, and video. -- -\n-- This approach ensures that even if the model does not have a large dataset initially, it can still provide accurate responses in natural language.\n\n-- The reward model considers the emotion and tone of the question and answer and continuously trains itself to improve accuracy.\n\n** Other Considerations\n-- The potential challenges or limitations of using ChatGPT technology, such as the risk of bias\n-- The importance of user testing and feedback in improving the system's accuracy and functionality\n-- The potential benefits of incorporating additional natural language processing (NLP) techniques or technologies into the system, such as sentiment analysis or named entity recognition\n-- The trade-offs involved in selecting different approaches to model training and selection, such as top K versus nucleus temperature\n-- The potential ethical considerations involved in designing a conversational agent, such as privacy concerns or the impact on employment in certain industries",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** ChatGPT Model\n-- A Transformer model is used, where the system predicts natural sequences of words. \n-- The model is trained on internet data such as websites, books, and Wikipedia links to provide semantically meaningful and grammatically correct replies.\n\nThe model can use multiple approaches such as top K, greedy, or nucleus temperature to select the most accurate prediction.\n\n** Chatbot Design\n-- A dataset of question-and-answer pairs is initially used to train the model.\n\n-- However, since training the model on every possible question-and-answer combination is impossible, a reward model is designed to select the best responses.\n\n-- The reward model is also trained using reinforcement learning, where the chatbot is rewarded for giving appropriate responses and penalized for inappropriate ones.\n\n-- The chatbot design is expected to support different input and output formats, including images, audio, and video. -- -\n-- This approach ensures that even if the model does not have a large dataset initially, it can still provide accurate responses in natural language.\n\n-- The reward model considers the emotion and tone of the question and answer and continuously trains itself to improve accuracy.\n\n** Other Considerations\n-- The potential challenges or limitations of using ChatGPT technology, such as the risk of bias\n-- The importance of user testing and feedback in improving the system's accuracy and functionality\n-- The potential benefits of incorporating additional natural language processing (NLP) techniques or technologies into the system, such as sentiment analysis or named entity recognition\n-- The trade-offs involved in selecting different approaches to model training and selection, such as top K versus nucleus temperature\n-- The potential ethical considerations involved in designing a conversational agent, such as privacy concerns or the impact on employment in certain industries",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
