      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- userId never shows up in a path or body. \nIt comes from the session token or JWT, and chat ownership is checked\nserver-side on every request. \n!!!! Passing userId in the body is a classic red flag, since anything the\nclient sends can be forged. The token stream uses SSE, ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- userId never shows up in a path or body. \nIt comes from the session token or JWT, and chat ownership is checked server-side on every request. \n!!!! Passing userId in the body is a classic red flag, since anything the client sends can be forged. The token stream uses SSE, ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
