      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786552846174,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) How to route and schedule generation requests across GPU workers",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) How to route and schedule generation requests across GPU workers",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "E_VBfltpeH7Nbx3HSJJhr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -507.4008992480701,
      "y": 2798.403153212491,
      "width": 1572.7180228072775,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b54",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1999025532,
      "version": 145,
      "versionNonce": 1822663748,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786552910341,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Queue + continuous batching and backpressure\n- Putting it together:\n1) The Chat Service enqueues a generation request with its runId and a token-cost estimate.\n2) Admission control checks queue depth. If we're over the limit, the request is shed or deferred (see the fairness\ndeep dive for who gets shed first).\n3) A GPU worker pulls the request and folds it into its running batch via continuous batching.\n4) The worker streams tokens to the runId stream as the batch generates.\n5) When generation finishes (or is cancelled), the worker drops the sequence from its batch and pulls the next\nrequest.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Queue + continuous batching and backpressure\n- Putting it together:\n1) The Chat Service enqueues a generation request with its runId and a token-cost estimate.\n2) Admission control checks queue depth. If we're over the limit, the request is shed or deferred (see the fairness deep dive for who gets shed first).\n3) A GPU worker pulls the request and folds it into its running batch via continuous batching.\n4) The worker streams tokens to the runId stream as the batch generates.\n5) When generation finishes (or is cancelled), the worker drops the sequence from its batch and pulls the next request.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Hj5A4i_tfnhCWN2KDMwQb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1938.2317610953794,
      "y": 1859.6918232332405,
      "width": 266.419921875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
