      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786553060516,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) How to keep heavy users from taking over GPU pool?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) How to keep heavy users from taking over GPU pool?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EyhO28UZqJIFmIpVqOhFx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -496.900565437998,
      "y": 3197.151943221439,
      "width": 1704.275146484375,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b58",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 279004612,
      "version": 202,
      "versionNonce": 808077124,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786553276696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--  The fix is to meter what's actually limited, which is tokens (or estimated compute), not request count. \nWhen a generation comes in, we estimate how expensive it'll be from the prompt length and the requested max output. \nWe check that against how much of the user's token budget is left and reject or delay it if they're over. \nThe budget refills over time, the way an API quota does. Now the thing we're counting is the thing we're actually paying for\n-- Paid users get bigger budgets, higher concurrency limits, and higher priority in the queue ==> Queue priority\nto distinguish and load\n-- When demand stills exceed capacity after admission control, free user are throttled, deferred or downgraded.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--  The fix is to meter what's actually limited, which is tokens (or estimated compute), not request count. \nWhen a generation comes in, we estimate how expensive it'll be from the prompt length and the requested max output. \nWe check that against how much of the user's token budget is left and reject or delay it if they're over. \nThe budget refills over time, the way an API quota does. Now the thing we're counting is the thing we're actually paying for\n-- Paid users get bigger budgets, higher concurrency limits, and higher priority in the queue ==> Queue priority\nto distinguish and load\n-- When demand stills exceed capacity after admission control, free user are throttled, deferred or downgraded.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7RACXB12FY359LSQTDsTM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -509.37283690589527,
      "y": 3485.795940049919,
      "width": 905.0716552734375,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
