      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786554139757,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4) Control inference cost without making assistant feel forgetful \n==> Prefix caching and summary update as conversation grows",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4) Control inference cost without making assistant feel forgetful \n==> Prefix caching and summary update as conversation grows",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "W_OTTc04PSHk1AJFTjDRT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -505.80933077221016,
      "y": 3561.2729188907397,
      "width": 1712.98291015625,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 896383428,
      "version": 107,
      "versionNonce": 1770308860,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786554149505,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- Prefix caching and rolling summary. Across turns in a single conversation, \nmost of the prompt is identical from one turn to the next.\nModern inference servers can cache the model's intermediate state (the KV cache) for a stable prompt prefix \nand reuse it instead of recomputing it from scratch every turn.\n-- The catch is that the cache has to be managed. A worker has finite memory and \ncan only keep so many conversations' prefixes warm at once, so prefixes are evicted on something like an LRU basis.\n-- The summary updates in the background as the conversation grows, folding the oldest verbatim turns in as they age out. \nThe two levers complement each other, with the summary keeping the prompt inside the window \nand prefix caching keeping the stable part cheap to process.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- Prefix caching and rolling summary. Across turns in a single conversation, \nmost of the prompt is identical from one turn to the next.\nModern inference servers can cache the model's intermediate state (the KV cache) for a stable prompt prefix \nand reuse it instead of recomputing it from scratch every turn.\n-- The catch is that the cache has to be managed. A worker has finite memory and \ncan only keep so many conversations' prefixes warm at once, so prefixes are evicted on something like an LRU basis.\n-- The summary updates in the background as the conversation grows, folding the oldest verbatim turns in as they age out. \nThe two levers complement each other, with the summary keeping the prompt inside the window \nand prefix caching keeping the stable part cheap to process.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
