      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 705777476,
      "version": 41,
      "versionNonce": 1092866684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786554146459,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- When the user hits stop, the client makes a plain HTTP call to POST /chats/{chatId}/runs/{runId}/cancel, \nexactly the side-channel we set aside when we chose SSE. \nThe Chat Service flips that Generation's status to cancelled and publishes a cancel signal \non a control channel keyed by the runId.\nThe worker checks that channel between token batches, \nand the moment it sees the signal it drops the sequence and stops generating.\n-- Cancellation immediately frees capacity that would otherwise stay occupied for the rest of the 30-second generation. \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- When the user hits stop, the client makes a plain HTTP call to POST /chats/{chatId}/runs/{runId}/cancel, \nexactly the side-channel we set aside when we chose SSE. \nThe Chat Service flips that Generation's status to cancelled and publishes a cancel signal \non a control channel keyed by the runId.\nThe worker checks that channel between token batches, \nand the moment it sees the signal it drops the sequence and stops generating.\n-- Cancellation immediately frees capacity that would otherwise stay occupied for the rest of the 30-second generation. \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
